const waveSection = `<section class="wrap section traffic-wave" id="traffic-wave" aria-labelledby="traffic-wave-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Try it · Traffic waves</p><h2 id="traffic-wave-title">Where phantom jams<br><em>come from.</em></h2></div><p>Twenty-two cars on a ring road, no bottleneck. Tap the brakes,<br class="desktop-break"> watch the slowdown ripple backward, then add automated vehicles.</p></div><div class="wave-stage"><canvas class="wave-ring" role="img" aria-label="Ring road with 22 cars. Red cars are slow or stopped; black cars with a white dot are automated. Click a car to make it brake."></canvas><div class="wave-chart-wrap"><p class="wave-chart-label">Each dot is a car’s position over time; red bands are stop-and-go waves moving backward.</p><canvas class="wave-chart" role="img" aria-label="Space-time diagram of every car’s position over the last 90 seconds"></canvas></div></div><div class="wave-controls"><button class="button wave-start" type="button" data-wave-start>Start</button><button class="wave-brake" type="button" data-wave-brake>Tap the brakes</button><div class="wave-av" role="group" aria-label="Automated vehicles in the traffic"><span>Automated vehicles</span>${[0, 1, 2, 4].map(n => `<button type="button" data-wave-av="${n}" aria-pressed="${n === 0}">${n}</button>`).join('')}</div><p class="wave-stats"></p></div><p class="sr-only wave-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="wave-note">Simulated at three times real speed. Human drivers follow the Intelligent Driver Model with a 0.6-second reaction delay; automated vehicles hold the average speed and keep a buffer, as in ring-road field tests.<br><a href="https://doi.org/10.1088/1367-2630/10/3/033001">Sugiyama et al., 2008 ${arrow}</a> <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trc.2018.02.005">Stern et al., 2018 ${arrow}</a></p></section>`;
